7 23.0227 16.1248 24.608 18.2509 26.8161C20.3959 29.0053 21.8823 31.8172 22.428 34.9501\" stroke=\"var(--meadow-accent-color)\" stroke-width=\"2.14929\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/>\n<path d=\"M1.50562 7.94373H11.5342\" stroke=\"var(--meadow-accent-color)\" stroke-width=\"2.14929\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/>\n<path d=\"M1.73071 2.24432H16.3691\" stroke=\"var(--meadow-accent-color)\" stroke-width=\"2.14929\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/>\n<path d=\"M1.73071 13.6622H7.77047\" stroke=\"var(--meadow-accent-color)\" stroke-width=\"2.14929\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/>\n</svg>\n</span> Notes</a></div>\n  <div class=\"wprm-layout-column-container wprm-column-gap-40 wprm-column-rows-recipe-900 meadow-main-columns\">\n    <div class=\"wprm-layout-column wprm-column-width-50 meadow-main-left\">\n      <div id=\"recipe-10643-ingredients\" class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredients-container wprm-recipe-10643-ingredients-container wprm-block-text-normal wprm-ingredient-style-regular wprm-recipe-images-before\" data-recipe=\"10643\" data-servings=\"8\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-ingredients-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-spacer wprm-header-has-actions wprm-header-has-actions\" style=\"\">Ingredients<div class=\"wprm-decoration-spacer\"></div>&nbsp;&nbsp;</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-internal-container wprm-internal-container-ingredients wprm-expandable-container wprm-expandable-expanded\" style=\"\"><div class=\"wprm-internal-container-toggle\"><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"false\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-show\" aria-label=\"Show Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,9.5 8,5 12.5,9.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"true\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-hide\" aria-label=\"Hide Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,6.5 8,11 12.5,6.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-ingredient-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: var(--meadow-accent-color);\">Ingredients</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ul class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredients\"><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">4</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">lbs</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">bone-in turkey breast</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">About 4 lbs.</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">2</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">tablespoons</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">olive oil</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">For rubbing on the turkey.</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">teaspoon</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">salt</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">To taste.</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1/2</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">teaspoon</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">black pepper</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">To taste.</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">teaspoon</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">garlic powder</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">For flavor.</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">teaspoon</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">dried thyme</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">For flavor.</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">teaspoon</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">paprika</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">For color and flavor.</span></li></ul></div></div></div>\n      <div id=\"recipe-10643-equipment\" class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-container wprm-block-text-normal\" data-recipe=\"10643\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-equipment-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none\" style=\"\">Equipment</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-internal-container wprm-internal-container-equipment wprm-expandable-container wprm-expandable-expanded\" style=\"\"><div class=\"wprm-internal-container-toggle\"><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"false\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-show\" aria-label=\"Show Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,9.5 8,5 12.5,9.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"true\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-hide\" aria-label=\"Hide Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,6.5 8,11 12.5,6.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a></div><ul class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment wprm-recipe-equipment-list\"><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">1 roasting pan&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">For roasting the turkey breast.</span></div></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">1 Oven&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">Preheat to 375°F (190°C).</span></div></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">1 Meat Thermometer&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">To check the internal temperature.</span></div></li></ul></div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"wprm-layout-column wprm-column-width-50 meadow-main-right\">\n      <div id=\"recipe-10643-instructions\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions-container wprm-recipe-10643-instructions-container wprm-block-text-normal\" data-recipe=\"10643\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-instructions-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-spacer wprm-header-has-actions\" style=\"\">Method<div class=\"wprm-decoration-spacer\"></div>&nbsp;</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-instruction-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: #000000;\">Instructions</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ol class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions\"><li id=\"wprm-recipe-10643-step-0-0\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 1: Preheat your oven to 375°F (190°C). This will ensure your turkey breast cooks evenly and thoroughly.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-10643-step-0-1\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 2: Pat the turkey breast dry with paper towels. This helps the skin get crispy. Rub the turkey evenly with olive oil for added flavor.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-10643-step-0-2\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 3: In a small bowl, mix together salt, black pepper, garlic powder, dried thyme, and paprika. This spice mixture will give your turkey a delightful taste.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-10643-step-0-3\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 4: Generously season the turkey breast all over with the spice mixture. Make sure to cover every nook and cranny for maximum flavor!</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-10643-step-0-4\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 5: Place the turkey breast on a rack in a roasting pan, skin side up. Roast in the preheated oven for 1½ to 2 hours, or until the internal temperature reaches 165°F (74°C) in the thickest part.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-10643-step-0-5\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 6: Remove the turkey from the oven and let it rest for 15 minutes. This allows the juices to redistribute. Then, slice and serve your delicious bone turkey breast!</span></div></li></ol></div></div>\n      \n      \n      <div id=\"recipe-10643-notes\" class=\"wprm-recipe-notes-container wprm-block-text-normal\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-notes-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none\" style=\"\">Notes</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-notes\"><table>\n<tr>\n<th>Nutrition Facts</th>\n<th>Per Serving</th>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Calories</td>\n<td>300</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Fat</td>\n<td>15g</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Protein</td>\n<td>40g</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Carbs</td>\n<td>0g</td>\n</tr>\n</table></div></div>\n      <div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 40px;\"></div>\n      \n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div></div></div>\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"ingredients\"><strong>Ingredients</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Gather these simple ingredients for a delicious bone <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Turkey_as_food\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">turkey </a>breast!</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"533\" src=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/Ingredients-for-Bone-Turkey-Breast-Recipe.webp\" alt=\"Ingredients for bone turkey breast displayed on a kitchen table.\" class=\"wp-image-10641\" srcset=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/Ingredients-for-Bone-Turkey-Breast-Recipe.webp 400w, https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/Ingredients-for-Bone-Turkey-Breast-Recipe-225x300.webp 225w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>bone-in turkey breast</strong> – about 4 lbs</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>olive oil</strong> – 2 tablespoons</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>salt</strong> – 1 teaspoon</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>black pepper</strong> – 1/2 teaspoon</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>garlic powder</strong> – 1 teaspoon</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>dried thyme</strong> – 1 teaspoon</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>paprika</strong> – 1 teaspoon</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"how-to-make-bone-turkey-breast\"><strong>How to Make bone turkey breast</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">This delicious bone turkey breast recipe is perfect for any occasion. With a preparation time of just 15 minutes and a cooking time of 1½ to 2 hours, plus an additional 15 minutes for resting, you&#8217;ll have a juicy and flavorful dish ready to impress your family and friends!</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"533\" src=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/Preparing-Bone-Turkey-Breast.webp\" alt=\"Step-by-step preparation of bone turkey breast, including preheating the oven, preparing the turkey, mixing spices, and roasting.\" class=\"wp-image-10642\" srcset=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/Preparing-Bone-Turkey-Breast.webp 400w, https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/Preparing-Bone-Turkey-Breast-225x300.webp 225w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 1: Preheat the Oven</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Preheat your oven to 375°F (190°C). This will ensure your turkey breast cooks evenly and thoroughly.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 2: Prepare the Turkey</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Pat the turkey breast dry with paper towels. This helps the skin get crispy. Rub the turkey evenly with olive oil for added flavor.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 3: Mix the Spice Blend</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">In a small bowl, mix together salt, black pepper, garlic powder, dried thyme, and paprika. This spice mixture will give your turkey a delightful taste.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 4: Season the Turkey</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Generously season the turkey breast all over with the spice mixture. Make sure to cover every nook and cranny for maximum flavor!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 5: Roast the Turkey</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Place the turkey breast on a rack in a roasting pan, skin side up. Roast in the preheated oven for 1½ to 2 hours, or until the internal temperature reaches 165°F (74°C) in the thickest part.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 6: Rest and Serve</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Remove the turkey from the oven and let it rest for 15 minutes. This allows the juices to redistribute. Then, slice and serve your delicious bone turkey breast!</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"recipe-snapshot\"><strong>Recipe Snapshot</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>Details</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Category</td><td>Main Course</td></tr><tr><td>Cuisine</td><td>American</td></tr><tr><td>Prep Time</td><td>15 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Cook Time</td><td>120 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Extra Time</td><td>15 minutes (resting)</td></tr><tr><td>Total Time</td><td>150 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Dietary</td><td>High Protein</td></tr><tr><td>Serves</td><td>8</td></tr><tr><td>Best Served</td><td>Warm with sides of your choice!</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"pro-tips-for-making-bone-turkey-breast\"><strong>Pro Tips for Making bone turkey breast</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Brine the turkey breast overnight for maximum juiciness.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Use a meat thermometer to ensure perfect doneness at 165°F.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Let the turkey rest for at least 20 minutes before carving.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Season under the skin for deeper flavor penetration.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Experiment with herbs like rosemary and thyme for a fragrant touch.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"how-to-serve-this-bone-turkey-breast\"><strong>How to Serve this bone turkey breast</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Slice and serve with a side of creamy mashed potatoes.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Pair with roasted seasonal vegetables for a colorful plate.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Top with homemade cranberry sauce for a sweet contrast.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Serve on a bed of wild rice for a hearty meal.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Use leftovers in sandwiches with lettuce and mayo for a tasty lunch.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Accompany with a fresh green salad drizzled with vinaigrette.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Offer a side of stuffing for a classic touch.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Garnish with fresh herbs for a pop of color and flavor.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"make-ahead-and-storage\"><strong>Make Ahead and Storage</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Storing and enjoying your bone turkey breast leftovers is easy!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Storing Leftovers</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Allow the turkey to cool completely before storing.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Wrap tightly in plastic wrap or aluminum foil.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Place in an airtight container for extra protection.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Store in the refrigerator for up to 3-4 days.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Freezing</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Slice the turkey breast for easier thawing.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Wrap each piece in plastic wrap, then in foil.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Label with the date and type of dish.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Freeze for up to 3 months for best quality.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Reheating</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Thaw in the refrigerator overnight before reheating.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Preheat the oven to 325°F (165°C).</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Cover with foil to retain moisture while reheating.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Heat until the internal temperature reaches 165°F (74°C).</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Explore more easy <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/breakfast/\"><strong>breakfast</strong></a> recipes, quick <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/lunch/\"><strong>lunch</strong></a> ideas, cozy <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/dinner/\"><strong>dinner</strong></a> meals, tasty <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/snacks/\"><strong>snacks</strong></a>, and delightful <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/dessert/\"><strong>dessert</strong></a>.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"fa-qs\"><strong>FAQs</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Here’s a helpful FAQ about this recipe:</p>\n\n\n<div id=\"rank-math-faq\" class=\"rank-math-block\">\n<div class=\"rank-math-list \">\n<div id=\"faq-question-1\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>1. How long do you cook a bone-in turkey breast?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>Cooking a bone-in turkey breast typically takes about 20 minutes per pound at 325°F. For example, a 6-pound turkey breast would take approximately 2 to 2.5 hours. Always use a meat thermometer to ensure it reaches an internal temperature of 165°F for safe consumption.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-2\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>2. Are bone-in turkey breasts good?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>Absolutely! Bone-in turkey breasts are known for their rich flavor and juiciness. The bone helps retain moisture during cooking, resulting in a tender and flavorful dish that’s perfect for any occasion.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-3\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>3. Is it better to cook a bone-in turkey breast at 325 or 350?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>Cooking at 325°F is generally recommended for bone-in turkey breasts as it allows for even cooking without drying out the meat. However, if you&#8217;re short on time, cooking at 350°F can also work, but be sure to monitor the internal temperature closely.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-4\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>4. Can you buy a bone-in turkey breast?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>Yes, bone-in turkey breasts are widely available at grocery stores, especially around the holiday season. You can also find them at butcher shops or order them online for delivery. Just make sure to check for freshness and quality before purchasing.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"final-thoughts\"><strong>Final Thoughts</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Cooking a bone-in turkey breast is not just a meal; it&#8217;s a delightful experience! Picture the aroma filling your kitchen as it roasts to perfection. This easy recipe promises juicy, flavorful slices that will have everyone coming back for seconds. So, roll up your sleeves, gather your loved ones, and enjoy this heartwarming dish together!</p>\n",
